    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d485-a2">

                <pb facs="0656" n="550" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg550"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Dawson to
                        the French chargé.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Santo
                                Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-01-29"><hi rendition="#italic">January 29,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Chargé d’affaires</hi>: I take real pleasure in
                    acknowledging the receipt of your polite note of yesterday, in which you so
                    kindly refer to the aid which the commanders of the U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eagle</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Paducah</hi> and
                    the acting American consular agent were fortunate enough to be able to give
                    French citizens during the recent revolutionary disturbances at Sanchez.</p>
                <p>I have sent a copy of your note to my Government in order that your thanks may be
                    transmitted to the American commanders through the regular channels, and also
                    sent another copy to Mr. Leroux.</p>
                <p>I improve the opportunity to have the pleasure of offering to you, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. C. Dawson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
